From: Pixel 2 Linux project
Subject: [PATCH] Capture stills with the Walleye rear camera flash

Open the IMX362 sensor and its linked two-channel flash device for a still
capture. Arm a bounded V4L2 software strobe so the PMIC switches both
outputs together. Use the sensor timing and captured buffer timestamp to
select the frame for the JPEG, and report errors to the original camera UI.
Enable the still shutter when the camera is ready to take the photo.

